// a range's `current()` is `V&`, so `foreach (0 .. $n as $i)` binds `$i` as `const usize&` when
// `$n` is a usize. `$i == 0` is then a borrow against an int32 literal - the array-key case in
// `key_compared_to_literal` is a `usize` *value* from `key()`, which is why that golden could not
// see this. Windows `console_write` is written this way, and codegen asserted i64 vs i32
usize $n = 3;

foreach (0 .. $n as $i) {
    if ($i == 0) {
        echo 1;
    }
    else {
        echo 0;
    }
}
